.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Container for drawing elements (lines, shapes, images, text) that can be rendered to a \fBPort\fP\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDrawing\fP contents are shared by nested drawings and animation attachments\&. \fBElementRef\fP retains its drawing contents, so elements remain editable while those owners exist\&. Nested drawing cycles are rejected\&. Persistent animation artwork is registered with Sprite\&.addAnimationDrawable(drawing, options); dynamic callbacks return a \fBDrawing\fP or null\&.

.PP
Port\&.drawDrawing(drawing, point, attributes) translates drawing coordinates by the point before applying the parent transform\&. Its rectangle overload maps the drawing's geometric bounds into that rectangle\&. Nested \fBDrawing\fP elements use the same bounds mapping\&. Native Quad/RotatedRect \fBDrawing\fP destinations require a finite affine parallelogram; degenerate source bounds retain unit scale on that axis\&. Inherited transforms and opacities do not mutate stored element \fBAttributes\fP\&. 
