.SS "\fBElementRef\fP addText (string text, \fBRect\fP rect, \fBAttributes\fP attrs)"

.PP
Add editable text to a drawing\&. Copies the text and attributes\&. Use font(), textSize(), textStyle(), fillColor() and fillOpacity() on the attributes to style it, as with \fBPort\&.drawText()\fP\&. Newlines are supported\&. The rectangle supplies the local layout bounds and four editable corner control points; hit testing uses that rectangle rather than glyph outlines\&. Element and parent transforms and opacities apply normally, including live attributes\&.

.PP
Text and styling are saved with drawing artwork in Part/Sprite snapshots\&. \fBFont\fP names and scaling factors are saved; font files are not embedded\&. The receiving system must provide the font for the same appearance\&. Older drawing snapshots remain readable\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItext\fP Text string, including the empty string; at most 1 MiB in UTF-8\&. 
.br
\fIrect\fP Finite rectangle with right >= left and bottom >= top, in drawing coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIattrs\fP Text styling and transformation attributes\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An \fBElementRef\fP of type \fBpdg\&.type_Text\fP for later editing\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Rendering requires a graphics build\&. In this example, sprite is an existing \fBSprite\fP; serializing it also saves the drawing assigned to its label \fBPart\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
var drawing = pdg\&.createDrawing();
var attrs = new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.font(pdg\&.gfx\&.createFont("Arial"))
    \&.textSize(24)\&.textStyle(pdg\&.textStyle_Bold)\&.fillColor("white");
var label = drawing\&.addText("Player 1", new pdg\&.Rect(0, 0, 180, 40), attrs);
sprite\&.createPart("label")\&.setDrawing(drawing);
label\&.setText("Player 2");
var save = new pdg\&.Serializer();
save\&.serialize_obj(sprite);

.fi
.PP
 
